  "note": "Self-written itemised medical bills and receipts (診療明細書・領収書 / itemised bill and receipt) for made-up clinics, hospitals and patients, with fictional amounts and no official form layout: an outpatient visit and a short hospital stay, each in a clean version and a planted one that differs only on the lines below. They run as business/proposal, the genre the payslips and utility bills run as: no genre is made for medical bills. Each mistake names its kind, the line it is on, the text the clean line has there (clean) and the planted line has instead (planted), and the rule expected to report it on that line; a mistake that breaks a pair of lines names the pair's other line as pairedLine. A line's points or units times the rate per point or unit is named for line-amount-mismatch, and the plant changes the points or units, not the amount, so the items still add up to the total. The total is planted in the charges table, not in the payment table, so it does not move the total the patient's share is compared with. A rule that does not exist yet is named as the rule that should: share-amount-mismatch (the amount a patient pays that is not the stated share, 3割 or 30%, of the total written beside it). A visit date after the issue date and a discharge date before the admission date are named for due-before-issue, which compares a pair of labelled dates on their own lines (date-range-reversed reads only a period written as one range). The days in hospital stated in the table and again in a sentence of the same section is named for fact-conflict. Each plant was also run alone on its clean document, so no plant depends on another. yarn planted medicalbills scores them; expected.json is the committed score.",
